1
00:00:01,269 --> 00:00:03,969
This is Contexo, a Visual Studio Code

2
00:00:03,969 --> 00:00:06,244
agent built on True Forge.

3
00:00:06,244 --> 00:00:08,169
It shows why code enters the model's

4
00:00:08,169 --> 00:00:10,794
context, puts edits up for review,

5
00:00:10,794 --> 00:00:12,344
and keeps the editor usable when a

6
00:00:12,344 --> 00:00:13,267
model fails.

7
00:00:15,490 --> 00:00:18,415
Task A. I select Flask's debug helper,

8
00:00:18,415 --> 00:00:20,335
press Command K, then E,

9
00:00:20,355 --> 00:00:22,330
and give the exact instruction.

10
00:00:22,330 --> 00:00:24,527
The request stays scoped to this function.

11
00:00:27,090 --> 00:00:29,715
The proposed change opens for review.

12
00:00:29,715 --> 00:00:31,440
I can reject a single hunk,

13
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:33,815
change my mind, and accept it.

14
00:00:33,815 --> 00:00:36,265
Contexo checks the base file hash and

15
00:00:36,265 --> 00:00:38,064
waits for Apply before writing.

16
00:00:44,090 --> 00:00:45,915
With Flask Debug set to off,

17
00:00:45,915 --> 00:00:47,405
the helper now prints False.

18
00:00:52,394 --> 00:00:54,914
In Changes, I undo the applied hunk.

19
00:00:54,914 --> 00:00:56,864
The original code comes back.

20
00:00:56,864 --> 00:00:58,840
Redo restores the reviewed change.

21
00:01:05,515 --> 00:01:07,190
I reset the demo checkout,

22
00:01:07,190 --> 00:01:09,740
start another request, and press Stop.

23
00:01:09,740 --> 00:01:12,065
Git status confirms the working tree stayed

24
00:01:12,065 --> 00:01:12,624
clean.

25
00:01:15,390 --> 00:01:17,365
Task B. I ask for a built-in

26
00:01:17,365 --> 00:01:20,240
Flask config command. The prompt names zero

27
00:01:20,240 --> 00:01:20,903
files.

28
00:01:24,080 --> 00:01:26,380
The context graph links the command,

29
00:01:26,380 --> 00:01:29,395
tests, and guide. The initial packet packs

30
00:01:29,395 --> 00:01:32,520
about sixty-nine hundred estimated source tokens into

31
00:01:32,520 --> 00:01:35,695
an eight-thousand-token budget. Below the graph you

32
00:01:35,695 --> 00:01:38,095
can inspect why excerpts were chosen,

33
00:01:38,095 --> 00:01:39,339
and which ones were left out.

34
00:01:51,869 --> 00:01:54,694
The TrueForge turn records the editor's MCP

35
00:01:54,694 --> 00:01:57,083
tools and the pending write approval.

36
00:01:59,670 --> 00:02:01,920
The proposal finds the implementation,

37
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:04,395
its tests, and the command guide.

38
00:02:04,395 --> 00:02:05,970
I review the hunks and then apply

39
00:02:05,970 --> 00:02:06,889
the changes.

40
00:02:12,265 --> 00:02:14,019
Sixty CLI tests pass.

41
00:02:16,815 --> 00:02:19,017
Flask help lists the new config command.

42
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:24,485
The demo app prints masked JSON.

43
00:02:24,485 --> 00:02:26,285
Even the nested key is masked,

44
00:02:26,285 --> 00:02:28,147
while public values stay readable.

45
00:02:31,385 --> 00:02:33,054
Git shows three changed files.

46
00:02:35,590 --> 00:02:38,365
Task C. I reset Flask and configure

47
00:02:38,365 --> 00:02:41,145
the primary model with an unreachable endpoint.

48
00:02:51,235 --> 00:02:53,285
I repeat the inline edit.

49
00:02:53,285 --> 00:02:55,085
The editor stays responsive,

50
00:02:55,085 --> 00:02:56,985
and a local Qwen model takes over

51
00:02:56,985 --> 00:02:57,896
automatically.

52
00:03:02,950 --> 00:03:05,519
The fallback's malformed write is rejected.

53
00:03:09,253 --> 00:03:11,603
Git status confirms the working tree stayed

54
00:03:11,603 --> 00:03:12,180
clean.

55
00:03:14,933 --> 00:03:16,733
Both routes are visible in the session

56
00:03:16,733 --> 00:03:18,671
view. I restore the primary.

57
00:03:25,465 --> 00:03:27,715
We also tried the local Bonsai four

58
00:03:27,715 --> 00:03:30,815
billion parameter checkpoint on LMCache.

59
00:03:30,815 --> 00:03:32,940
It read the selected file through True

60
00:03:32,940 --> 00:03:36,165
Forge. A separate retrieval test found all

61
00:03:36,165 --> 00:03:38,440
five target file roles within the transport

62
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:38,917
limit.

63
00:03:43,615 --> 00:03:46,065
TrueForge runs the agent loop.

64
00:03:46,065 --> 00:03:49,140
Contexo supplies the editor tools and context,

65
00:03:49,140 --> 00:03:51,090
gates every edit through review,

66
00:03:51,090 --> 00:03:53,365
and preserves a trace of each run.

67
00:03:53,365 --> 00:03:54,521
That's Contexo.
